    {
      "id": "3bdf895081fde1bdec7b9c5bb2d74d09277841b2",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2693982611,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I would guess this would be an optimization to speed up packet analysis if you didn't care about the http2 content, but this MR only has the creation of the preference, no actual use of it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-19T02:22:16.022Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-19T02:22:16.022Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 407354628,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20892,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "22cf7775019b28a10dc51f04bc59e23bc7108075",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2695024628,
          "type": null,
          "body": "One use case would be where the payload is a zip bomb where decompressing can cause a potential DoS (#13779). This needs to actually be used, though (including making sure Follow Stream output would still work, though now back to being compressed - #18239).",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-19T11:12:38.061Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-19T11:12:38.061Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 407354628,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20892,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "eb76d619c5303abadb3c0278a7127aa492dffa95",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2734246902,
          "type": null,
          "body": "To quickly follow up here, in my particular use-case I wanted to get the before/after sizes of the data. This was a nice-to-have obviously and not a deal-breaker; it mostly just seemed like an oversight given http/1 supported this flag but not http/2. Happy to close this MR if there's no desire for this one!",
          "author": {
            "id": 2389932,
            "username": "mikekap",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Mike Kaplinskiy",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fb629820cf3c0913b572152dcf49936571aaea9e334f3db3aed92a26b4f71109?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mikekap"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-06T22:19:21.389Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-09-06T22:19:21.389Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 407354628,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20892,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7896d38d7cba7947f74126a16c14d12d9d5f2edc",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2734249327,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Well, it could be useful, but it should possibly only define the preference if one of the compression libraries is present (which they probably are).\n\nThe MR doesn't change the use of the preference because a global is already defined based on the presence of the libraries.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-06T22:37:15.463Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-09-06T22:37:15.463Z",
