    {
      "id": "7b0cca5d098d049e9e81631826819a92783fc6f4",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2734517703,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I agree with @johnthacker that when reviewed, I didn't realize the boolean was already defined and this is probably a good change.  I rebased it and added support for when the decompression libraries are supported.  When \"not supported\", I think considering it an \"obsolete\" preference will continue to save the value if switching between systems that may not have decompression libraries (although this is unlikekly).",
